# -*- encoding: utf-8 -*-
# Arc: StoryBeginnings | Scene: MeetingKateInTheGarden

translate es strings:

    old "Sarah slowly walked through the castle's garden. A thin blanket of snow covered most of the plants."
    new "Sarah caminaba lentamente por el jardín del castillo. Una fina capa de nieve cubría la mayoría de las plantas."

    old "She sat down on one of the benches, drawing Varga's cloak tighter around herself."
    new "Se sentó en uno de los bancos, apretando el manto de Varga más contra sí misma."

    old "Sarah offered to give the cloak back, but now, sitting in the snow-covered garden, she was happy he had been too polite to accept."
    new "Sarah ofreció devolver el manto, pero ahora, sentada en el jardín cubierto de nieve, estaba feliz de que hubiera sido demasiado cortés para aceptarlo."

    old "She wondered what to make of him. Accomplished beyond his years, and still, seemingly embarassed for his lowborn origins."
    new "¿Qué pensaba de él? Un prodigio que había superado a su edad, y sin embargo, parecía vencido por la vergüenza ante sus humildes orígenes."

    old "Sarah had met enough nobility to know that titles were a poor replacement for a good heart."
    new "Sarah había conocido a suficientes nobles como para saber que los títulos son un pobre sustituto de un buen corazón."

    old "A twig snaps behind her."
    new "Una rama se rompe detrás de ella."

    old "Sarah spun around towards the source of the sounds."
    new "Sarah giró hacia la fuente de los sonidos."

    old "Standing a little distance off is a woman with grey hair, and soft white skin as if she could fade into the snow."
    new "Un poco más lejos se encuentra una mujer con el cabello gris y la piel blanca y suave, como si pudiera desvanecerse en la nieve."

    old "Something about her seems...familiar."
    new "Algo de ella parece... familiar."

    old "Hey Sarah, been a while."
    new "¡Hola Sarah, ha pasado un tiempo."

    old "Sarah stares at the woman, trying to figure out how she knows her."
    new "Sarah observa a la mujer, tratando de averiguar cómo la conoce."

    old "Then, it dawns on her."
    new "Entonces, se le ocurre."

    old "Kate!!"
    new "¡Kate!"

    old "Sarah jumps off the bench and runs towards the woman, leaping into an embrace."
    new "Sarah se lanza del banco y corre hacia la mujer, arrojándose en un abrazo."

    old "I was starting to worry you didn't remember me!"
    new "¡Empecé a preocuparme por si no me recordabas!"

    old "Kate laughs."
    new "Kate ríe."

    old "Wow, I just...I can't believe this. It's really you."
    new "Wow, solo... no puedo creerlo. Eres tú de verdad."

    old "Sarah takes a step back, still holding onto Kate. She eyes her up and down, almost as if afraid she isn't real."
    new "Sarah da un paso atrás, aún sosteniendo a Kate. La mira de arriba abajo, como si temiera que no sea real."

    old "You've changed so much..."
    new "Has cambiado tanto..."

    old "Kate had been Sarah's closest friend in childhood."
    new "Kate había sido la mejor amiga de Sarah desde la infancia."

    old "Unlike Sarah, Kate had been born to a servant family, working in the castle, but when they were children, matters of class weren't important."
    new "A diferencia de Sarah, Kate nació en una familia de sirvientes y trabajaba en el castillo, pero cuando eran niñas, los temas de clase no importaban."

    old "They had explored every corner of the castle together, for years, they had been inseparable."
    new "Habían explorado cada rincón del castillo juntos durante años; habían sido inseparables."

    old "Then, one day, Kate and her family were just gone."
    new "Entonces, un día, Kate y su familia simplemente desaparecieron."

    old "Sarah had been devastated. She asked her father to find her friend, but after months had gone by with no news, she had to move on."
    new "Sarah había quedado devastada. Le pidió a su padre que encontrara a su amiga, pero tras pasar meses sin noticias, tuvo que seguir adelante."

    old "Her father had tried to comfort her, telling her that this was not unusual for servants, to simply leave for work elsewhere, but Sarah had always kept wondering where her friend went."
    new "Su padre intentó consolarla, diciéndole que esto no era inusual para los sirvientes, simplemente irse a trabajar en otro lugar, pero Sarah siempre se había preguntado dónde fue su amiga."

    old "And now, after years, she stood right in front of her."
    new "Y ahora, después de años, se paraba justo frente a ella."

    old "Older by quite a bit, of course, but Sarah could easily identify the features of her friend and how they had developed into maturity."
    new "Mucho mayor, por supuesto, pero Sarah podía identificar fácilmente las facciones de su amiga y cómo habían evolucionado hasta la madurez."

    old "You're one to talk...just look at you. I remember when you were as flat-chested as a boy."
    new "Tú misma... mira quién lo dice. Recuerdo cuando tenías los pechos planos como los de un niño."

    old "Sarah felt herself turn red."
    new "Sarah sintió cómo se le ponía la cara roja."

    old "Still as crude as always, I see."
    new "Todavía tan vulgar como siempre, veo."

    old "Yeah, I missed out on all the classes on how to be a lady, sorry."
    new "Sí, me perdí todas las clases de cómo ser una dama, lo siento."

    old "Sarah looks at her old friend. All grown up, but it was like she never left."
    new "Sarah mira a su vieja amiga. Ya adulta, pero es como si nunca hubiera partido."

    old "Where did you go..."
    new "¿A dónde fuiste..."

    old "Sarah's tone had grown more serious. Half a question, half an accusation. How could you leave me like that, she wanted to ask."
    new "El tono de Sarah se había vuelto más serio. Media pregunta, media acusación. ¿Cómo podías dejarme así?, quería preguntar."

    old "Kate turned away, searching for the words."
    new "Kate se volvió buscando las palabras."

    old "We were friends, Sarah, but you didn't know everything about me. About my life."
    new "Fuimos amigas, Sarah, pero no sabías nada de mí. De mi vida."

    old "Kate sighs."
    new "Kate suspira."

    old "But you're right, I do owe you an explanation."
    new "Pero tienes razón, sí te debo una explicación."

    old "My life wasn't the same as yours. My family didn't come from money..."
    new "Mi vida no era lo mismo que la tuya. Mi familia no provenía del dinero..."

    old "I knew that, and I never treated you any differently for it."
    new "Lo sabía, y nunca te traté de manera diferente por ello."

    old "Kate shakes her head."
    new "Kate sacude la cabeza."

    old "No, that's not what I mean."
    new "No, no es eso lo que quiero decir."

    old "She pauses for a moment."
    new "Hace una pausa por un momento."

    old "When we were growing up, we were free to do as we pleased, but as we grew older, more and more was expected of us. You noticed it too."
    new "Cuando éramos jóvenes, podíamos hacer lo que nos diera la gana, pero a medida que crecíamos, se esperaban de nosotros cada vez más cosas. Tú también lo notaste."

    old "Sarah nodded."
    new "Sarah asintió."

    old "For you that meant taking classes, riding horses, learning how to be a princess."
    new "Para ti eso significaba tomar clases, montar a caballo y aprender a ser una princesa."

    old "For me, it meant that my parents began to expect me to start working. Preparing me for what I was going to be. A servant in the castle..."
    new "Para mí, significaba que mis padres comenzaron a esperar que empezara a trabajar. Preparándome para lo que iba a ser: una sirvienta en el castillo..."

    old "Kate took a longer pause, struggling to speak."
    new "Kate tomó una pausa más larga, luchando por hablar."

    old "And it meant becoming...a wife."
    new "Y eso significaba convertirse... en una esposa."

    old "Kate let her words hang in the air."
    new "Kate dejó que sus palabras colgaran en el aire."

    old "Sarah noticed how Kate had lingered on the word wife. As if there was some special significance to that fact."
    new "Sarah notó cómo Kate se había detenido en la palabra esposa, como si ese hecho tuviera algún significado especial."

    old "My family was preparing me for a life I never wanted. Being a poor kid, that I could handle, but the idea of becoming like my parents. Slaving away in some castle, for someone else, I didn't want to even think about it."
    new "Mi familia me estaba preparando para una vida que nunca quise. Ser una niña pobre, eso lo podía manejar, pero la idea de acabar como mis padres: trabajando como esclavo en algún castillo por cuenta de otros... no quería ni pensarlo."

    old "A lot happened at home, and I never let you see any of that. I didn't think you would understand."
    new "Muchas cosas han sucedido en casa, y nunca te dejé ver ninguna de ellas. No pensé que las entenderías."

    old "Kate looked to the ground. She seemed ashamed to admit that she had thought so low of her friend."
    new "Kate miró al suelo. Parecía avergonzada de admitir que había pensado tan mal de su amiga."

    old "I suffered through it, growing up, pretending like it wasn't going to happen. That if I ignored it, it wouldn't be real. That worked for a while, because when I was with you, it was easy to forget the rest."
    new "Yo sufrí todo eso creciendo, fingiendo que no iba a pasar. Que si lo ignoraba, no sería real. Eso funcionó por un tiempo, porque cuando estaba contigo, era fácil olvidar el resto."

    old "Kate looked straight at Sarah."
    new "Kate miró directamente a Sarah."

    old "And then, one night, they brought over a man. Must have been, twice my age. And they told me he had recently lost his wife, and that he was looking for a new wife."
    new "Y entonces, una noche, trajeron a un hombre. Debe de haber tenido el doble de mi edad. Y me dijeron que había perdido recientemente a su esposa y que estaba buscando una nueva."

    old "Sarah felt her chest tighten as her friend shared her grief."
    new "Sarah sintió cómo su pecho se apretaba mientras su amiga compartía su dolor."

    old "He was rich, by my family's standards. He would take care of me, they said. I would be provided for. And though they didn't say it, with me out of the house, it would be one less mouth to feed."
    new "Era rico, según los estándares de mi familia. Él se encargaría de mí, decían. Yo estaría provista. Y aunque no lo dijeron, conmigo fuera de casa, sería una boca menos que alimentar."

    old "Kate looked past Sarah."
    new "Kate miró más allá de Sarah."

    old "Sarah could see Kate's eyes, they seemed suddenly vacant, as if Kate was lost in a deep memory. Not just recalling, but reliving."
    new "Sarah podía ver los ojos de Kate; parecían vacíos de repente, como si Kate estuviera perdida en un recuerdo profundo. No solo recordando, sino reviviendo."

    old "As my parents were telling me all this, I could feel, somewhere in the root of my soul that I would never be able to survive a life like that."
    new "Mientras mis padres me contaban todo esto, sentía, en lo más profundo de mi alma, que jamás podría sobrevivir a una vida así."

    old "Some people can accept the torture that life inflicts on them, carry that burden...endure. I just knew that if I went with that man, I would not survive it."
    new "Algunas personas pueden aceptar la tortura que la vida les inflige, cargar con esa carga... soportarla. Solo sabía que si me iba con ese hombre, no sobreviviría a ello."

    old "And so, that very night, as I could hear my parents bargain my life away in the next room, I gathered what little I had, and snuck out the house."
    new "Así que, esa misma noche, mientras podía oír a mis padres regatear mi vida en la habitación de al lado, reuní lo poco que tenía y me escapé de la casa."

    old "Kate looked back at Sarah again."
    new "Kate volvió a mirar a Sarah."

    old "I tried to go to you, I swear, I wanted to tell you everything."
    new "Intenté ir a ti, lo juro, quería contarte todo."

    old "Kate almost seemed to beg Sarah."
    new "Kate parecía casi suplicar a Sarah."

    old "But I knew that if I did, your father would have just had his soldiers bring me back. For months after, I cried, knowing what I did to you."
    new "Pero sabía que si lo hacía, tu padre habría mandado a sus soldados a traerme de vuelta. Durante meses después lloré, sabiendo lo que te hice."

    old "Kate's eyes had begun to well up."
    new "Los ojos de Kate comenzaron a llenarse de lágrimas."

    old "Sarah embraced her friend and could feel the warmth of Kate's tears on her cheek, cutting through the cold."
    new "Sarah abrazó a su amiga y pudo sentir el calor de las lágrimas de Kate en su mejilla, cortando el frío."

    old "Kate began to sob, and Sarah drew her friend in closer."
    new "Kate comenzó a sollozar y Sarah la abrazó con más fuerza."

    old "After a moment, Kate regained her composure, and struggled on with her story."
    new "Después de un momento, Kate recuperó la compostura y continuó con su relato."

    old "After that, I wandered around for a long time. I lived off the kindness of strangers for a long time."
    new "Después de eso, vagué por mucho tiempo. Viví de la amabilidad de los extraños durante mucho tiempo."

    old "One day, I was begging at a town square, when a band of soldiers entered the town."
    new "Un día, estaba mendigando en una plaza cuando entró un grupo de soldados en la ciudad."

    old "Riding at the front was this man- Ooh Sarah, you won't believe me, but it was like the sun's light fell on him and lingered. He was radiant."
    new "Al frente cabalgaba ese hombre... Oh, Sarah, no podrás creerlo, pero era como si la luz del sol cayera sobre él y se quedara allí. Era radiante."

    old "Kate's voice had begun to pick up, full of excitement."
    new "La voz de Kate había comenzado a subir de tono, llena de entusiasmo."

    old "A crowd of people gathered to watch them, and I couldn't keep away. I was drawn in like everyone else."
    new "Una multitud de gente se había reunido para observarlos, y no pude apartarme. Me atraía como todos los demás."

    old "He looked across the crowd and his eyes fixed on me. I could hardly hear him over all the people, but I saw his mouth move, and Sarah, I swear on our friendship, he called out my name."
    new "Miró a través de la multitud y sus ojos se fijaron en mí. Apenas podía oírlo entre tanta gente, pero vi moverse sus labios, y Sarah, juro por nuestra amistad, que llamó mi nombre."

    old "This man I had never met before, he knew me, out of thousands, and called me to him."
    new "Este hombre que nunca había conocido me conocía, entre miles, y me llamó a mí."

    old "Kate's eyes welled up again, but these were tears of pure ecstasy."
    new "Los ojos de Kate se llenaron de lágrimas otra vez, pero estas eran lágrimas de puro éxtasis."

    old "I came forward and fell to my knees before him. He pulled out a sword, this one actually."
    new "Avanzé y me arrodillé ante él. Sacó una espada, esta de verdad."

    old "Kate pointed to the sword on her hip."
    new "Kate señaló la espada en su cadera."

    old "And he threw it down in front of me."
    new "Y la arrojó frente a mí."

    old "He told me that I had found what I was looking for, and all I had to do was pick up the sword and swear my loyalty to him."
    new "Me dijo que había encontrado lo que buscaba y que solo tenía que agarrar la espada y jurar lealtad a él."

    old "And I did, Sarah. With all my heart, I swore to him that I would be true."
    new "Y lo hice, Sarah. Con todo mi corazón, le juré que sería fiel."

    old "Kate paused, gathering her breath from the excitement, she had been speaking so fast."
    new "Kate se detuvo para recuperar el aliento tras tanta emoción; había estado hablando tan rápido."

    old "His name is Vaelen, and he's the leader of a mercenary company called \"Brothers of Providence\". Since that day, I've served him as best as I could."
    new "Su nombre es Vaelen, y es el líder de una compañía mercenaria llamada \"Hermanos de la Providencia\". Desde ese día, le he servido lo mejor que pude."

    old "Sarah had listened attentively to her friend."
    new "Sarah escuchó atentamente a su amiga."

    old "She could understand Kate's motivations, but she wasn't sure what to make of the last part of her story. All she could see was that Kate seemed happy just telling her about it."
    new "Podía comprender las motivaciones de Kate, pero no estaba segura de qué hacer con la última parte de su historia. Todo lo que podía ver era que Kate parecía feliz solo por contárselo."

    old "Kate...I'm just so happy to see you again, and to know that you've been okay all these years."
    new "Kate... estoy tan contenta de verte otra vez y de saber que has estado bien todos estos años."

    old "Travelling around the world, every now and again, I would hear news from Rosanna, and I would learn you were doing good."
    new "Kate: Viajando por todo el mundo, de vez en cuando oía noticias de Rosanna y aprendía que estabas bien."

    old "It was unfair that you never had that certainty about me. Ooh Sarah, if I could make this up to you, I would."
    new "Era injusto que nunca tuvieras esa certeza sobre mí. Oh Sarah, si pudiera compensarte por esto, lo haría."

    old "Sarah shook her head firmly."
    new "Sarah negó con la cabeza firmemente."

    old "Put all that behind you. Whatever there is to be forgiven, consider it forgiven. Seeing you again, on a day like this, it seems like fate."
    new "Déjalo todo atrás. Todo lo que haya por perdonar, considéralo perdonado. Volver a verte en un día como este parece el destino."

    old "Kate came closer and grasped Sarah's hands."
    new "Kate se acercó y agarró las manos de Sarah."

    old "I'll admit Sarah, it's not fate. When the news of your father's death came to me, I knew that I had to return, as sure as I once knew I had to leave this place."
    new "Lo admito, Sarah, no es el destino. Cuando llegó la noticia de la muerte de tu padre, supe que tenía que volver, con la misma certeza con la que antes sabía que tenía que abandonar este lugar."

    old "I just had this image in my mind, of you, all alone in this lifeless castle, and it wouldn't stop tormenting me until I had set out on the road, back to you."
    new "Solo tenía esta imagen en mi mente, de ti, todo/a sola en este castillo sin vida, y no paraba de atormentarme hasta que me puse en camino hacia ti."

    old "Sarah squeezed her friend's hands."
    new "Sarah apretó las manos de su amiga."

    old "I'm not alone."
    new "No estoy sola."

    old "The two old friends embraced."
    new "Los dos viejos amigos se abrazaron."

    old "Sarah broke away from the embrace, remembering her duties."
    new "Sarah se separó del abrazo, recordando sus deberes."

    old "I need to go back inside, I've been away for too long...poor Thomas, he's in there all by himself."
    new "Necesito volver adentro... he estado fuera demasiado tiempo... pobre Thomas, está solo en el interior."

    old "I understand."
    new "Entiendo."

    old "Please, don't leave though. Stay, stay in the castle and come visit me. I'll ask the servants to prepare you a room."
    new "Por favor, no te vayas. Quédate, quédate en el castillo y ven a visitarme. Preguntaré a los sirvientes que preparen una habitación para ti."

    old "Kate smiled at Sarah."
    new "Kate sonrió a Sarah."

    old "Thank you, Sarah, that means a lot to me."
    new "Gracias, Sarah, eso significa mucho para mí."

    old "Sarah waved to her friend as she went back inside. She ordered the servants to prepare a guest room and went back to the great hall."
    new "Sarah saludó a su amiga mientras regresaba al interior. Ordenó a los sirvientes que prepararan una habitación para invitados y volvió al gran salón."
